Z||000000||87 Steve GT||02-17-2000||11:30 PM||||With all that talk about the turn signal project.... I got to thinking,which at times can get me in trouble... VENT LGHTS..  =)<P>I mounted on a small bracket.. one just above my air cleaner.. (V6).. and the other just above my battery, I use (made) small bracket's to hold the light's in place, and so that I would'nt hurt air flow out of the vent's...  I used round(2") standard red clearance light's... <P>I just directly wired them to my parking(tail) light's, so when i hit my switch inside they come on with my parking light's.....  MAN THEY REALLY GLOW AT NIGHT.. YOU CAN SEE THEM FOR 30 Feet.... and the best part is I can not see them at all from inside because the vent's point to the rear...  will try to get a pic soon... Steve||||reg||6
Z||000001||stimpy||02-17-2000||11:52 PM||||Oh... That is cool!<BR>Do you mind if I crib that idea? <BR>I will trade you my cool plenum badge concept.  I just picked up GM part #22658817, the V6-H.O. badge on the front fenders of the new Grand Am. It is a very cool looking replacement for that hokey fiero decal on the non-engraved plenums.||||reg||1
